    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d196">

                <pb facs="0190" n="184" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg184"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Uhl to Mr.
                            Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-04-27"><hi rendition="#italic">April 27,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your dispatch of the 11th
                    instant, concerning the enforcement of the Bering Sea regulations and calling
                    attention to the use of the word “exclusive” in section 1 of the act approved
                    April 6, 1894.</p>
                <p>For your information, I inclose copy of the Department’s note of the 18th
                        instant<anchor n="1" xml:id="d196-f1"/> on this subject to the British
                    ambassador at the capital, together with six copies of an act of Congress,
                    approved April 24, 1894, wherein the error referred to is corrected.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin F. Uhl</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
